    "result_text": "The sheet's due-total and overdue-total now leave out the single highest and single lowest person's figure when three or more people have one. `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests.\n\nI made the change in two places, because the totals are worked out in both:\n- **Screen** (`src/main/frontend/src/app/features/people/people.ts`): the totals row works out the trimmed sums, and the header gets its figures from there. A person whose due-total is `n/a` isn't counted, and everyone's overdue-total is counted.\n- **Server** (`src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/rollup/RollupService.java`): the `TOTALS` audit line uses the same trimmed sums. A `TOTALS` line is still written only when a total actually changes. So a change can now move one person's figures without changing the trimmed totals, and then there is no `TOTALS` line. The test expects this, for example after the cap is set.\n\nPer-person figures, the per-grade and per-period totals, backing and the claimed total are not trimmed. No stored data or schema needed to change.",
